ain-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/20689-wraith-ghosts-in-space?p=970811#post970811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/20689-wraith-ghosts-in-space?p=970775#post970775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I really want to do something with a Heretic UFO cult.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just &quot;live&quot; the right kind of post-life and there's no need to seek Transcendence! Transcendence will come for YOU!</div> </div> </div> </div>One could even mix and match them with the Thal'Hun society from Sorcerer 1st edition (that were kind of ganked hard &amp; replaced with some &quot;truth is out there, we'll show you!&quot; nuts in Revised, unfortunately).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:17:40-07:00","id":972766,"title":"","content":"I'm certain that I've read in some book about spectres in the Tempest being able to get thrown through nihils into what is effectively the Deep Umbra and come back earthward into the other levels of the Umbra to cause mischief. Not sure if it wa<i>s in The Book of Worlds</i> from the Mage line, <i>Sea of Shadows</i>, or some other Wraith book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T04:36:46-07:00","id":973039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/20689-wraith-ghosts-in-space?p=972766#post972766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm certain that I've read in some book about spectres in the Tempest being able to get thrown through nihils into what is effectively the Deep Umbra and come back earthward into the other levels of the Umbra to cause mischief. Not sure if it wa<i>s in The Book of Worlds</i> from the Mage line, <i>Sea of Shadows</i>, or some other Wraith book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That should make for some particularly crazy trip indeed, specially if Wraiths somehow find the same path, or a group of garou or fae tried to follow them back from where they came...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:41:43-07:00","id":973948,"title":"","content":"My homebrew rule is wraiths can &quot;visit&quot; extraterrestrial places if there are &quot;fetter&quot;, for example people living in a extraterrestrial base by Void Engineers. Space ships &quot;relics&quot; can be used like vehicles in the underworld, but they can't travel to the Umbra, or it is too risky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T17:14:13-07:00","id":975742,"title":"","content":"I would allow the Wraith a limited ability to explore space, especially if there are people living there (on spacefraft in orbit, manned space stations, future space colonies). However, it would only be a matter of time before the Tempest &quot;swallowed up&quot; the Wraith which would probably lead to discorporation and reforming of the Wratih at his fetters unless the Wraith is highly skilled at Argos and can somehow make his way back to a safer spot of the Tempest. The likelihood of local maelstroms would be very high.<br /> <br /> &quot;Shadowlands&quot; can only really exist where the living are present, and space right now does not have enough people living in it to make it safe for wraiths to exist there. Most of the time, it is going to be a very dangerous part of the Tempest as Nihils and Barrow Flames constantly pop up at night, if meteors are present, if solar flames erupt, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T09:08:43-07:00","id":977204,"title":"","content":"Spaces coloniaes are possible by the Technocracy, but the gaulent or barriers would be too hard to allow visits by wraiths who lived there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T09:11:07-07:00","id":977205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/20689-wraith-ghosts-in-space?p=977204#post977204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spaces coloniaes are possible by the Technocracy, but the gaulent or barriers would be too hard to allow visits by wraiths who lived there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's questionable if any of the games that aren't Mage exist in a setting where the Technocracy exists and has space colonies, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T11:56:52-07:00","id":977279,"title":"","content":"Besides, the idea of a haunted space station is kind of too fun (imo) to just write off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}